Compiling OpenSSL and iproute2 inside /sources

1. Navigate to the sources directory and download OpenSSL:

`cd /sources`
`curl -O https://www.openssl.org/source/openssl-3.2.1.tar.gz`

2. Extract and build OpenSSL:

`tar -xf openssl-3.2.1.tar.gz`
`cd openssl-3.2.1`
`./config --prefix=/usr --openssldir=/etc/ssl --libdir=lib shared zlib-dynamic`
`make -j$(nproc)`
`make install`
`cd /sources`
`rm -rf openssl-3.2.1*`

3. Download iproute2 for core networking support (ip, ss):

`curl -O https://mirrors.edge.kernel.org/pub/linux/utils/net/iproute2/iproute2-6.8.0.tar.xz`

4. Extract and build iproute2:

`tar -xf iproute2-6.8.0.tar.xz`
`cd iproute2-6.8.0`
`configure --prefix=/usr`
`make -j$(nproc)`
`make install`

5. Clean up the build workspace:

`cd /sources`
`rm -rf iproute2-6.8.0*`
